                    "time": "2026-02-12T09:08:30+01:00"
                  },
                  "message": "Substitute \"-\" with \"\\-\"\n\nThe previous behavior is to emit “-” literally when encountered in the\ninput stream.\n\nWhen using man(1) from mandoc(1), it renders “-” (U+002D HYPHEN-MINUS),\nbut when using man(1) from man-db, it renders as “‐” (U+2010 HYPHEN).\n\ngroff_char(7) says:\n\n    The hyphen-minus is a particularly unfortunate case of overloading.\n    Its awkward name in ISO 8859 and later standards reflects the many\n    distinguishable purposes to which it had already been put by the\n    1980s, including a hyphen, a minus sign, and (alone or in\n    repetition) dashes of varying widths.\n\n    For best results in roff systems, use the “-” character in input\n    outside an escape sequence only to mean a hyphen, as in the phrase\n    “long‐term”.\n\n    For a minus sign in running text or a Unix command‐line option dash,\n    use \\- (or \\[-] in groff if you find it helps the clarity of the\n    source document).\n\nSince scdoc has no way of determining whether a “-” in the input stream\nshould be a hyphen, a minus sign, a Unix command‐line option dash, or\nelse, it’s safer to emit overall “\\-” so users don’t have issues\nsearching or copying Unix command‐line options.\n\nReferences: https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports/-/issues/17936\n",
                  "parents": [
                    {
                      "id": "1c36cde87212494368ea218e871085ed2bc855fe"
                    }
                  ]
